                <pb facs="0356" n="262" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg262"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Sir Julian Pauncefote to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy,<lb/>Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1896-03-23"><hi rendition="#italic">March 23,
                                1896</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 6th
                    ultimo, suggesting that a record be kept by the masters of British sealing
                    vessels of all female nursing seals killed in Bering Sea during the coming
                    season, I have the honor to inform you that I have received a communication from
                    Her Majesty’s Government stating that they are in correspondence with the
                    Government of Canada on the subject of this proposal.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Julian
                    Pauncefote.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
